# Auth and sessions

Login (Better Auth cookie) is not the same thing as a Google access token (~1h). Do not mix them.

## Login

- Google sign-in requests **identity only**. Extra APIs (Calendar, Drive, …) go on a later `linkSocial` with scopes — never on `socialProviders.google.scope`.
- Use `prompt: "select_account"`, never `"consent"` on sign-in. Consent re-lists previously granted extra scopes.
- Use `accessType: "offline"` so the first grant / new scopes can store a refresh token.
- Always pass `errorCallbackURL` on `signIn.social`. Set `onAPIError.errorURL` to the web app.
- Honor `callbackUrl` from the proxy (must start with `/`).

## Session cookies

- `expiresIn` must stay **≤ 400 days** (Chrome / better-call). Larger values 500 the OAuth callback. Do not set “100 years”.
- Use sliding sessions: `expiresIn` + `updateAge` + `deferSessionRefresh: true`.
- **Never refresh cookies on the server.** Next RSC, proxy, server actions, and Hono `auth.api.getSession` cannot apply `Set-Cookie` to the browser. That desyncs the session and looks like logout on the next navigation.
- Server `get-session`: `disableRefresh=true`, `credentials: "omit"`. Treat HTTP 200 + JSON `null` as logged out.
- Server Hono client: `credentials: "omit"`; forward the browser `Cookie` header only.
- Proxy: `getSessionCookie` only. Do not call `get-session`.
- Slide expiry in the browser via `SessionRefresher` (`authClient.useSession()`).

@see https://www.better-auth.com/docs/concepts/session-management#defer-session-refresh
@see https://www.better-auth.com/docs/integrations/next#auth-protection
